  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1549",
      "html": "<p>Trichomycterus mondolfi (Schultz, 1945). Size: 61 mm SL. Viewed from the side, there are two broken bands running the length of the body.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1549",
      "html": "<p>South America: Tuy River basin in Venezuela. Type locality: Quebrada Chacaito near Caracas, Estado de Miranda, Río Tuy system.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1549",
      "html": "<p>Found in nature alongside tetras, Chaetostoma spp., and small Rhamdia.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1549",
      "html": "<ul><li>pH: 6.6–7.4</li><li>Temperature: 23–25°C</li><li>Water should be well oxygenated.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1549",
      "html": "<p>A substrate of gravel and sand decorated with medium and large well-rounded stones.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1549",
      "html": "<p>Live, frozen and dry foods are readily accepted.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1549",
      "html": "<p>Peaceful with smaller tankmates. This species is not a parasite.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1549",
      "html": "<p>Unreported in the aquarium.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1549",
      "html": "<p>This catfish is only known from a handful of streams around Caracas. Pollution and development are destroying the last few natural habitats of this fish. It will likely be extinct by 2020 or sooner.</p>"
    },
